Hydra render delegate must honor PointInstancer-level visibility

Hiding a PointInstancer prim (token visibility = "invisible") is honored in VP2 and
HdStorm but was ignored by the Arnold Hydra render delegate, which kept rendering the
instances. HdArnoldInstancer now gates instance creation on the instancer's Hydra
visibility (sceneDelegate->GetVisible), matching hdSt / hdPrman.

The scene has two PointInstancers: InvisibleInstancer (hidden, on the right) must not
render any instances, while VisibleInstancer (on the left) must still render all of
its instances - guarding against the fix over-hiding visible instancers.

Fixes #2715

author: cyril.pichard@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'scene':'scene.usda', 'diff_hardfail': 0.04}
